<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n8555" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">clāvĭcŭla</span></b> ,
			ae, f.
		dim.
		id. * <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A small key</i>, <i><span class="en">Caes. Germ.
				Arat. 195</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A tendril</i>, <i>by which the vine
				clings to its props</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Sen.
				15, 52</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. N. D. 2, 47, 120</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Col. 4, 6,
			2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 23</span></i>, prooem. §
			5.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>A bar</i>, <i>bolt of the door</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Hyg. Grom. 55</span></i>.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">clāvĭcŭlārĭus</span></b> ,
				ĭi, m., <i>a
				key-keeper</i>, <i>jailer</i>, Firm. Math. 3,
		66.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
</div>